From 557e694fc799a83d1a4d321764c8a410dc40669a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:44:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 701/702] SableOS: pure contact-list letter and number model
 for Phone

Plain Java (no android.* types) behind the Sable Phone contacts list:

* SableAlphabetIndex maps a letter to list positions inside the
  address-book index the list already carries (section titles and
  counts from ContactsProvider). Accents fold to their base letter,
  sections that start with no letter are never targets, and pressing
  the same letter again cycles through its rows and wraps.
* SablePreferredNumbers is a bounded, read-only, in-memory map from
  contact id to the number shown under the name: the default number
  (IS_SUPER_PRIMARY) first, then the account primary, then the first
  row; at most 5000 contacts from at most 20000 provider rows; blank
  or over-long numbers skipped. Never written back or persisted.
* SableSubtitle formats "Mobile . number" with the number in Unicode
  left-to-right isolates.
* SableListKeys decides what a typed character does on the list:
  letters jump (never open, call or edit), "/" opens search where
  there is one, held keys do nothing, modified keys and everything
  else keep their upstream meaning, and nothing applies while search
  or selection is active.

Host tests live in the SableOS Q25 repository under
tests/framework/packages/apps/Dialer.
